**Game Design Document: Fantasy Quest**

**Game Overview**

Fantasy Quest is a text-based adventure game set in the realm of Elvendom. The game allows players to navigate through a fantasy world, interact with non-player characters, and make choices that affect the game outcome. The goal of the game is to reach the fabled Golden Scepter.

**Game Architecture**

The game will be built using object-oriented programming principles in Python. The game will consist of the following classes:

- **Game**: This class will serve as the main class of the game. It will handle the game loop, input/output operations, and game state management.
- **Player**: This class will represent the player character. It will have properties such as health, location, and inventory.
- **NPC**: This class will represent non-player characters. It will have properties such as name, description, and interaction methods.
- **World**: This class will represent the game world. It will have methods for navigating the game world and interacting with NPCs.

**Game Mechanics**

- **Game Loop**: The game loop will consist of the main menu, game world, and game over screen.
- **Input/Output**: The game will use a text-based interface for input/output operations.
